  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows positive bias (e.g., >0.00) and model overestimates prices.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent true outcomes show mean reversion toward lower levels after a spike.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or negative (e.g., <0.00), especially if model has overcorrected upward.",
    "Apply lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast 3-5 days ago, adjust current forecast downward by 3-7%.",
    "Avoid overshoot after sharp price spikes: if model forecasts >10% above recent peak, reduce by 15-25% to align with historical volatility patterns.",
    "Use sentiment as a momentum filter: if sentiment >0.50, model should be more conservative; if <0.00, allow for slight upward adjustment to reflect bearish reversal."
  ]
}
